# d27_named_groups / spellings.rxt
#
# PROMISE under test: the three named-capturing-group declaring
# spellings -- (?<name>...), (?'name'...), (?P<name>...) -- create an
# ORDINARY capturing group at its left-to-right number. Match behavior
# and capture spans are identical to the unnamed (...) form; only the
# reflection surface (rx_info.groups/nnames -- not exercised by this
# file's m/g mechanic, see README) differs.
#
# Oracle: python3 `re` only accepts the (?P<name>...) spelling; every
# (?<name>...) / (?'name'...) case below is oracle-verified on its
# (?P<name>...) translation by oracle.py. All spans/group indices below
# were computed from that translation (see oracle.py's own output).

# --- baseline: unnamed group, for direct comparison with the named
# forms below. Already supported today (no module needed). ---
pattern (a)
m "xax" 1 2
g 1 1 2

# --- same shape, three declaring spellings, must match the baseline
# above span for span ---
pattern (?<n>a)
features named-groups
m "xax" 1 2
g 1 1 2

pattern (?'n'a)
features named-groups
m "xax" 1 2
g 1 1 2

pattern (?P<n>a)
features named-groups
m "xax" 1 2
g 1 1 2

# --- quantified named group: same span the unnamed form gives, and the
# cross-iteration retention rule (docs/spec/match_api.md S5.1) applies
# to a named group exactly as it does to a numbered one: the group
# keeps its span from the last iteration in which it ran ---
pattern (a)+
m "xaaax" 1 4
g 1 3 4

pattern (?<n>a)+
features named-groups
m "xaaax" 1 4
g 1 3 4

pattern (?'n'a)+
features named-groups
m "xaaax" 1 4
g 1 3 4

pattern (?P<n>a)+d
features named-groups
m "xaaadx" 1 5
g 1 3 4

# --- alternation branches, mixed declaring spellings in ONE pattern:
# each branch's named group gets its own left-to-right number; the
# spelling chosen per branch does not matter to numbering or capture ---
pattern (?<a1>x)|(?P<b1>y)
features named-groups
m "x" 0 1
g 1 0 1
g 2 -1 -1

pattern (?<a1>x)|(?P<b1>y)
features named-groups
m "y" 0 1
g 1 -1 -1
g 2 0 1
